
Project Overview
This project will establish a data-driven feedback loop between product design and manufacturing quality inspection. We will develop an ontology and knowledge graph to ingest, harmonize, and compare "as-designed" part data with "as-inspected" data from various suppliers.
Task Plan
Phase 1: Foundation & Proof of Concept 
•	Design and formalize a core ontology that defines key entities, their attributes, and their relationships.
•	Develop and test Python scripts to parse the provided QIF files, extract design and inspection data, and transform it into RDF triplets according to the ontology.
•	Instantiate a graph database, load the generated triplets for the target part, and verify data.
•	Develop and execute foundational SPARQL queries to compare design vs. inspection data.
Phase 2: Expansion & Insight Generation
•	Enhance the ETL pipeline to ingest and harmonize QIF inspection data from extended set of QIF standard, validating the ontology.
•	Develop SPARQL queries to identify patterns, such as the most frequently failed characteristics, and correlations between deviations and specific suppliers.
•	Work on a technical approach and roadmap to automate the data extraction process from Siemens Teamcenter.
Deliverables
1.	QIF Design & Inspection Ontology File (in OWL/TTL format).
2.	ETL Source Code with documentation.
3.	A populated Proof-of-Concept Knowledge Graph instance.
4.	baseline SPARQL queries to compare design and inspection information.
1.	Knowledge Graph REST API & Teamcenter integration approach 

